# Norris Writer — Product Vision

This is the author's list of what Norris Writer should be. Preserve these when refactoring or cutting IDE features. Add new items here as the product evolves.

## Must have

### 1. Git in each story folder

Each story (novel, series book, etc.) lives in its own folder with its own Git repository for version history, drafts, and branches — not a single repo for the whole workspace.

- Keep SCM/Git enabled (`git.enabled`, Source Control view).
- Support opening a story folder as the workspace root so Git scopes to that story.
- Do not remove merge/conflict tooling needed for Git workflows.

### 2. The editor (current setup)

Keep the writing editor experience as configured today unless the author explicitly asks to change it.

Current defaults (`norrisWriter.contribution.ts`):

- Markdown opens in the rich markdown editor (`*.md` → `vscode.markdown.editor`).
- Writing View: formatted text while editing (`norrisWriter.markdown.alwaysRendered`).
- Paper appearance (`norrisWriter.editorAppearance` → Paper).
- Word count in the status bar (`norrisWriter.wordCount.enabled`).
- Activity bar on top; chat in the secondary sidebar.
- AI chat available (TokenMix / Norris Writer chat integration).

### 3. The Explorer

Keep the file Explorer sidebar for navigating story folders, chapters, notes, and assets.

- Do not remove the Explorer viewlet or file tree.
- Authors organize manuscripts as files and folders; the Explorer is primary navigation.

### 4. Workbench UI is the writing tool

Do not remove the workbench shell: activity bar, sidebar views (Explorer, Search, SCM, Outline, Timeline), editor area, panels, command palette, Settings, Extensions view (VSIX install), and chat panel.

Explicitly keep for AI: embedded browser (`browserView`), voice agents, MCP plugin UI.

## Nice to have

- Timeline sidebar (Git + local file history per chapter)
- Outline sidebar (heading navigation in long markdown files)

## Explicitly not goals

- Full IDE for software development (debug, terminal, tasks, remote, TypeScript language server, programming-language grammars)
- Jupyter notebooks (`.ipynb`)
- Microsoft account sign-in (`microsoft-authentication` removed; GitHub auth kept for Git)
- Extension marketplace browse (VSIX install only unless gallery added later)
